    "script": "<p><span style=\"font-size:18pt;\"><strong>[[EXPERIMENT_TITLE]] - Loading Isotherm Determination Report</strong></span></p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:14pt;\">Experiment Information</span></h4>\n<p><strong>Experiment ID:</strong> [[EXPERIMENT_ID]]</p>\n<p><strong>Start Date:</strong> [[EXPERIMENT_DATE]]</p>\n<p><strong>End Date / Report Generated:</strong> [[REPORT_DATE]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:14pt;\">Objective</span></h4>\n<p>Determination of loading isotherms for <strong>[[LIGAND_NAME]]</strong> on the selected resin at different salt concentrations (<strong>[[SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</strong>) using an automated robotic workflow. The aim is to quantify bound ligand per gram of resin across a range of feed concentrations (<strong>[[LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</strong>) under defined buffer conditions (<strong>[[BUFFER]]</strong>).</p>\n<p> </p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:14pt;\">Methods</span></h4>\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Overview of Automated Workflow</span></h5>\n<p>The experiment was executed on an integrated automated platform combining an Opentrons OT-2 liquid handler, a UR5 robotic arm, a vacuum manifold with controlled pump, and a Tecan Spark platereader. The process was designed to perform equilibration, loading, incubation, filtration, and absorbance-based quantification for multiple salt and ligand concentration conditions.</p>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Key Experimental Parameters</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Process ID:</strong> [[PROCESS_ID]]</li>\n<li><strong>Resin mass per well:</strong> [[RESIN_MASS]]</li>\n<li><strong>Buffer:</strong> [[BUFFER]]</li>\n<li><strong>Salt:</strong> [[SALT_NAME]]</li>\n<li><strong>Salt stock concentration:</strong> [[SALT_STOCK_CONCENTRATION]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</li>\n<li><strong>Salt concentrations in experiment:</strong> [[SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]] (total: [[NUMBER_OF_SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]])</li>\n<li><strong>Ligand name:</strong> [[LIGAND_NAME]]</li>\n<li><strong>Ligand stock concentration:</strong> [[LIGAND_STOCK_CONCENTRATION]] [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</li>\n<li><strong>Ligand concentrations in experiment:</strong> [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]] (total: [[NUMBER_OF_LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]])</li>\n<li><strong>Total volume per well:</strong> [[TOTAL_VOLUME]]</li>\n<li><strong>Incubation temperature:</strong> [[INCUBATION_TEMPERATURE]]</li>\n<li><strong>Incubation time:</strong> [[INCUBATION_TIME]]</li>\n<li><strong>Shaker speed during incubation:</strong> [[SHAKER_SPEED_INCUBATION]]</li>\n<li><strong>Number of technical replicates per condition:</strong> [[REPLICATES]]</li>\n<li><strong>Measurement wavelength:</strong> [[MEASUREMENT_WAVELENGTH]] nm</li>\n<li><strong>Calibration curve:</strong> slope = [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_SLOPE]], intercept = [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_INTERCEPT]]</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Automated Equilibration of Resin</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Resin was pre-dispensed into a 96-deep-well plate (\"96DeepWP\") with [[RESIN_MASS]] resin per well.</li>\n<li>The UR5 robotic arm transferred the deep-well plate from storage to the vacuum manifold position.</li>\n<li>A 96-well filter plate (\"Filterplate\") containing the resin bed was placed on the Opentrons OT-2 deck (custom labware: <em>cytiva_96_filterwellplate_1ml</em>).</li>\n<li>The OT-2 executed equilibration protocols, adding equilibration buffer (<strong>[[BUFFER]]</strong>) with a total volume of [[EQUILIBRATION_VOLUME]] per cycle.</li>\n<li>The UR5 moved the filter plate onto the vacuum manifold, and the vacuum pump was applied at <strong>[[PUMP_SPEED]]</strong> for <strong>[[PUMP_DURATION]]</strong> per cycle to drain the wells.</li>\n<li>After each pump step, a venting period of <strong>[[VENTING_TIME]]</strong> was applied to allow pressure equilibration.</li>\n<li>The equilibration sequence was repeated for <strong>[[EQUILIBRATION_CYCLES]]</strong> cycles, each with a duration of [[EQUILIBRATION_CYCLE_DURATION]].</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Automated Ligand Loading and Incubation</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Following equilibration, the filter plate was returned to the OT-2 deck.</li>\n<li>The OT-2 prepared and dispensed ligand solutions of <strong>[[LIGAND_NAME]]</strong> at defined concentrations (<strong>[[LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</strong>) at varying salt concentrations (<strong>[[SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]</strong>) into the equilibrated resin-containing wells, ensuring a total volume of [[TOTAL_VOLUME]] per well.</li>\n<li>The plate was incubated at <strong>[[INCUBATION_TEMPERATURE]]</strong> for <strong>[[INCUBATION_TIME]]</strong> with shaking at <strong>[[SHAKER_SPEED_INCUBATION]]</strong> to reach adsorption equilibrium.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Filtration and Collection of Flow-Through</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li>After incubation, the UR5 transferred the deep-well plate and filter plate to the vacuum manifold.</li>\n<li>The vacuum pump was again applied at <strong>[[PUMP_SPEED]]</strong> for <strong>[[PUMP_DURATION]]</strong> with a subsequent venting period of <strong>[[VENTING_TIME]]</strong> to collect clarified flow-through samples in the receiver plate.</li>\n<li>The UR5 returned the receiver plate containing the flow-through (\"96DeepWP\" at OT2_Pos5) to the OT-2 deck for subsequent processing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Preparation of Measurement Plate and Spectrophotometric Readout</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li>The UR5 placed a fresh 96-well plate (\"WP1\") on the OT-2 deck.</li>\n<li>The OT-2 transferred defined volumes of flow-through from the receiver deep-well plate into \"WP1\".</li>\n<li>The UR5 moved \"WP1\" into the Tecan Spark platereader.</li>\n<li>The Tecan Spark performed absorbance measurements at <strong>[[MEASUREMENT_WAVELENGTH]]</strong> nm using the pre-defined method.</li>\n<li>After measurement, \"WP1\" was returned to storage by the UR5.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Data Processing</span></h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Flow-through absorbance values were converted to equilibrium ligand concentrations using the calibration curve (slope [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_SLOPE]], intercept [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_INTERCEPT]]).</li>\n<li>Loaded ligand per gram of resin was calculated from the mass balance between loaded and residual ligand, normalized by <strong>[[RESIN_MASS]]</strong> and the total volume [[TOTAL_VOLUME]].</li>\n<li>Loading isotherms were generated for each salt concentration and fitted to appropriate adsorption models as needed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:14pt;\">Results</span></h4>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Loading Isotherms at Different Salt Concentrations</span></h5>\n[[PLOT_1]]\n<p><em>Figure 1: Loading isotherms of [[LIGAND_NAME]] on the resin at different salt concentrations ([[SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]]). Each curve represents equilibrium loading (q) versus equilibrium ligand concentration (c) derived from flow-through measurements at [[MEASUREMENT_WAVELENGTH]] nm (calibration: slope [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_SLOPE]], intercept [[CALIBRATION_CURVE_INTERCEPT]]).</em></p>\n\n<h5><span style=\"font-size:12pt;\">Summary of Experimental Design</span></h5>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:99.9866%;\" border=\"1\">\n<tr>\n<th>Parameter</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Number of salt concentrations</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[NUMBER_OF_SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] ([[SALT_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[SALT_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]])</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Number of ligand concentrations</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[NUMBER_OF_LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]] ([[LIGAND_CONCENTRATIONS]] [[LIGAND_CONCENTRATION_UNIT]])</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Replicates per condition</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[REPLICATES]]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Resin mass per well</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[RESIN_MASS]]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Equilibration cycles</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[EQUILIBRATION_CYCLES]] (volume [[EQUILIBRATION_VOLUME]], cycle duration [[EQUILIBRATION_CYCLE_DURATION]])</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Pump settings</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Speed [[PUMP_SPEED]], duration [[PUMP_DURATION]], venting time [[VENTING_TIME]]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Incubation conditions</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Temperature [[INCUBATION_TEMPERATURE]], time [[INCUBATION_TIME]], shaker speed [[SHAKER_SPEED_INCUBATION]]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">Measurement wavelength</td>\n<td style=\"height:22.3828px;\">[[MEASUREMENT_WAVELENGTH]] nm</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p> </p>\n<h4><span style=\"font-size:14pt;\">Notes</span></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>All steps described above were executed using the integrated robotic workflow (Opentrons OT-2, UR5, vacuum manifold, Tecan Spark) as defined in the process script for this experiment.</li>\n<li>Raw data, processing scripts, and fitted model parameters for the loading isotherms are stored in the associated data records for [[EXPERIMENT_ID]].</li>\n</ul>\n",
